# Git on Windows converts line endings to CRLF on checkout by default. For a repository that
# ends up inside a Linux container that is not cosmetic but a failure: run.sh starts with a #!
# line, and with a \r behind it the kernel looks for a program that does not exist
# ("bad interpreter"). The add-on then refuses to start, with an error that points nowhere near
# the real problem.
#
# eol=lf therefore keeps everything LF -- in the repository and in the working copy, on every
# machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binary files.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.bin binary
